      "message": "* **Leaky Abstraction in `UsbComm` Endpoints:** In `usb_comm.h`, `kEpOutBulk` (0x01) and `kEpInBulk` (0x81) are globally hardcoded, and `UsbComm::Send()` explicitly routes traffic to `kEpOutBulk`. However, `BootromComm` bypasses `Send()` entirely and calls `usb_.BulkWrite()` directly because it needs to write to endpoint `0x02` (`kBootromEpOutBulk`).  \n    \n* **Suggestion:** Remove the hardcoded endpoints from `UsbComm`. Make endpoints configurable either via the constructor `UsbComm(ctx, vid, pid, ep_in, ep_out)` or by passing them directly into `Send()` and `Receive()`.",
      "range": {
